      "body": "## Overview\n\nThe `baidu/Unlimited-OCR` checkpoint renamed its `model_type`, which breaks two AMD CI steps on current main. This registers both the old and the new spelling.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes `(MI355 DPX) Basic Models (Extra Initialization) Shard 1` and `(MI355 DPX) Multimodal Processor Shard 4`, failing in [build 94688](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/94688/list) and every build since.\n- Keeps checkpoints pinned to a revision from before the rename working.\n- No behaviour change for any other model: four registry entries, no new logic.\n\n## Validation\n\nFive tests across `test_initialization.py`, `test_tensor_schema.py` and `test_common.py` fail on current main and pass with this change, verified on gfx950:\n\n```\npytest tests/models/test_initialization.py \\\n       tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_tensor_schema.py \\\n       tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_common.py \\\n       -k Unlimited -q\n```\n\nBefore: `4 failed, 662 deselected` and `1 failed, 401 deselected`. After: all pass.\n\n## Details\n\nThe failure looks like this:\n\n```\npydantic_core._pydantic_core.ValidationError: 1 validation error for ModelConfig\n  Value error, The repository baidu/Unlimited-OCR contains custom code which must\n  be executed to correctly load the model.\nPlease pass the argument `trust_remote_code=True` to allow custom code to be run.\n```\n\nNo vLLM commit caused it. The hub checkpoint changed: commit [`8249d20b`](https://huggingface.co/baidu/Unlimited-OCR/commit/8249d20b2822a7d8a4c22c8d8c9069b5ac36bda3), \"Update files for compatibility with transformers (#13)\", renamed `model_type` from `unlimited-ocr` to `unlimited_ocr`. Every commit on that repository since June had only touched the README.\n\nvLLM ties this model to four registries, all keyed on `model_type` by exact string match. `_maybe_register_hf_config` therefore no longer finds `UnlimitedOCRConfig`, so it is never registered with `AutoConfig`, and transformers falls back to the repository's `auto_map`. That `auto_map` has always been present; it only started to matter once the lookup began to miss.\n\nBoth spellings are registered rather than just renamed, because `_register_config_class` assigns `model_type` from whichever key matched, so a revision pinned before the rename keeps resolving.\n\nOne limitation worth naming: the same hub commit also added `chat_template.jinja`, so the new chat template fallback entry is inert for current revisions. I added it anyway so that all four registries agree on the model type rather than leaving one keyed only on the old name.\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
